# Per-instance paths for ONE Vocalis install.  Copy to `vocalis.env` and edit.
#
# 🔴 THE POINT OF THIS FILE: systemd reads it via `EnvironmentFile=`, and the hand-run
# maintenance tools read it themselves (tts_utils.load_env_file).  One source of truth, so the
# service and the tools CANNOT disagree about which install's data they are touching.
#
# Without it, these values live only as `Environment=` lines in the unit — which a shell does
# not inherit.  Running `src/vault_migrate.py` over SSH then resolves the cache to whichever
# install owns ~/.cache/vocalis, reports on THAT instance, and offers to clear it.
#
# Only needed if you run more than one Vocalis on this box, or want non-default locations.
# A single install with default paths needs no file at all.
#
# Format is systemd's EnvironmentFile subset: KEY=VALUE, `#` comments, no shell expansion —
# write absolute paths, NOT $HOME or ~.  Nothing here overrides a variable already exported.

# The cache: MD5 audio cache + chunk workspaces.
# 🔴 Defaults to ~/.cache/vocalis — keyed on WHO IS LOGGED IN, not on where Vocalis is
# installed, so two installs collide here by default.  This is the one that bites.
VOCALIS_CACHE_DIR=/home/youruser/.cache/vocalis-myinstance

# Where plaintext is allowed to touch disk (5.0 §8.3).  Swept at startup.
# Defaults to <install root>/work/scratch, which is already per-install — override to put it
# on a dm-crypt volume or a faster disk.
VOCALIS_SCRATCH_DIR=/scratch/vocalis-myinstance

# The Applio workspace used for voice training.
# 🔴 Defaults to ~/Applio — also keyed on $HOME, so two installs collide here too, and unlike
# the cache there is NO runtime guard that catches it.  They just train into one workspace.
VOCALIS_APPLIO_DIR=/home/youruser/Applio-myinstance
